  + [required_field] is fixture_id
  + [required_field] is input_source_ref_set
  + [required_field] is expected_record_kind
  + [required_field] is expected_record_id_pattern
  + [required_field] is expected_natural_key_state
  + [required_field] is expected_subject_ref_state
  + [required_field] is expected_authority_state
  + [required_field] is expected_source_ref_set_state
  + [required_field] is expected_lineage_edge_set_state
  + [required_field] is expected_freshness_state
  + [required_field] is expected_record_status
  + [required_field] is expected_blocked_or_fault_reason
  + [required_field] is acceptance_status

  = must: make expected candidate records reviewable without reading generated SQLite
  = must: require explicit expected blocked or fault reason when extraction cannot safely complete

& [ExpectedSQLiteProjectionLedgerShape] is the expected SQLite projection ledger shape
  + [required_field] is fixture_id
  + [required_field] is expected_projection_table_set
  + [required_field] is expected_projection_row_count_by_table
  + [required_field] is expected_source_hash_columns_present
  + [required_field] is expected_authority_state_columns_present
  + [required_field] is expected_freshness_state_columns_present
  + [required_field] is expected_projection_status_columns_present
  + [required_field] is expected_generated_artifact_set
  + [required_field] is expected_non_authority_notice
  + [required_field] is expected_rebuild_or_refusal_state
  + [required_field] is acceptance_status

  = must: treat expected SQLite ledgers as tracked SOP expectations, not the generated database
  = must: prove generated database deletion and rebuild does not erase authority

& [ExpectedValidationLedgerShape] is the expected validation ledger shape
  + [required_field] is fixture_id
  + [required_field] is validation_subject_ref
  + [required_field] is expected_hash_check_status
  + [required_field] is expected_signature_check_status
  + [required_field] is expected_lineage_check_status
  + [required_field] is expected_freshness_check_status
  + [required_field] is expected_authority_classification
  + [required_field] is expected_proof_result_status
  + [required_field] is expected_fault_or_interrupt
  + [required_field] is proof_limit
  + [required_field] is acceptance_status

  = must: distinguish structural validation from semantic truth
  = must: make missing evidence, stale evidence, wrong protocol, and ambiguous identity visible

& [NoAuthorityPromotionProofChecklist] is the fixture proof checklist for source/projection separation
  + [proof_check] is source SOP fixture remains tracked authority
  + [proof_check] is expected-output ledger remains tracked authority
  + [proof_check] is generated parser output remains projection-only
  + [proof_check] is generated SQLite output remains projection-only
  + [proof_check] is generated cache or report output remains projection-only
  + [proof_check] is generated projection cannot supply SJS satisfaction signature
  + [proof_check] is generated projection cannot satisfy source_manifest requirement
  + [proof_check] is source mutation attempt produces fault or refusal output
  + [proof_check] is stale or invalid fixture case cannot become ready output
  + [proof_check] is operations control and live machine control remain absent

& [FixtureExecutionPolicy] is the future fixture execution policy
  + [future_command] is python -m unittest tests.test_ir2_parser_projection_contracts
  + [baseline_command] is python -m unittest discover -s tests
  + [compile_command] is python -m compileall -q src tests
  + [generated_output_policy] is future tests may write only tests/fixtures/generated/ir2_parser_projection/ and .langsop/ generated paths
  + [cleanup_policy] is generated fixture outputs may be deleted and rebuilt

  = must: require future implementation tests to prove no source mutation and no authority promotion
  = must: fail fixture execution if generated outputs are required as source authority

